# Desculpting Blast, {1}{U}: "Return target nonland permanent to its owner's hand. If it was attacking, create a 1/1 colorless Drone artifact
# creature token with flying and 'This token can block only creatures with flying.'" Bot2 attacks Bot1 with its Ornithopter on turn 4; Bot1
# (the caster, not the attacker's controller) returns it with the attack declared: it goes to Bot2's hand and Bot1 gets the Drone.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Desculpting Blast
Island x17

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Island x19

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T4 Bot2.DeclareAttackers]
Bot2.Attack(Ornithopter > Bot1)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Desculpting Blast.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Drone Token.Power = 1
? Bot1.Battlefield.Drone Token.Toughness = 1
? Bot1.Battlefield.Drone Token.Types = Artifact; Creature
? Bot1.Battlefield.Drone Token.Colors = (absent)
? Bot1.Battlefield.Drone Token.Keywords = CanBlockOnlyCreaturesWithFlying; Flying

[Expect]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Power = 0
Bot2.Battlefield.Count = 0
Bot1.Life = 20
